ypothetical FAO report might indicate that Bolivia produces around</span> 40,000 <span class ="tr_" id="tr_30" data-source="" data-orig="tons per year">tons per year</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_31" data-source="" data-orig="Peru approximately">Peru approximately</span> 30,000 montones, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_32" data-source="" data-orig="with the remainder coming from smaller producers">with the remainder coming from smaller producers</span> .</p><h3 class="" data-start="1392" data-end="1423"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="Emerging_Production_Zones"></span><span class ="tr_" id="tr_33" data-source="" data-orig="Emerging Production Zones">Emerging Production Zones</span><span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h3><p class="" data-start="1424" data-end="1712"><span class ="tr_" id="tr_34" data-source="" data-orig="In addition to traditional producers">In addition to traditional producers</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_35" data-source="" data-orig="regions in North America">regions in North America</span>, Europa, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_36" data-source="" data-orig="and Asia have started experimenting with quinoa cultivation">and Asia have started experimenting with quinoa cultivation</span>. <span class ="tr_" id="tr_37" data-source="" data-orig="These emerging markets are driven by local demand and technological advances">These emerging markets are driven by local demand and technological advances</span>, <span class ="tr_" id="tr_38" data-source="" data-orig="gradually adding diversity and flexibility to the global quinoa supply chain">gradually adding diversity and flexibility to the global quinoa supply chain</span>.</p><hr class="" data-start="1714" data-end="1717" /><h2 class="" data-start="1719" data-end="1754"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="2_Varieties_of_Quinoa_by_Region"></span>2. <span class ="tr_" id="tr_39" data-source="" data-orig="Varieties of Quinoa by Region">Varieties of Quinoa by Region</span><span class="ez-toc-section-end"></sp